Qore ZIP module packages
========================

This development snapshot targets qore-testing, not general release. Runtime
includes native bindings, source/AOT ZipDataProvider, qzip, metadata, resources
and all translations; the doc package contains both references and test examples.
Debug symbols cover the native library, private minizip and AOT provider.

Ubuntu 26.04 minizip-ng 4.0.10 is built without AES, BZip2, LZMA/XZ or Zstandard.
The source package therefore contains a private minizip-ng 4.2.2 component with
all advertised features, including the upstream symlink-extraction correction.
It links system zlib, BZip2, liblzma, Zstandard and OpenSSL. minizip symbols are
hidden; no minizip headers, static libraries, CMake files or shared ABI are installed.
The existing ENGINE compatibility patch is applied to a build copy and failures
are fatal. The checked-out submodule is never modified. PPMd is not exposed by
this module and is disabled. No build-time downloads are permitted.

Source preparation
------------------

Export tracked module files except debian/ and src/minizip-ng to
qore-zip-module_1.0.0~git20260928.1+ds.orig.tar.xz with the matching top-level
directory, then copy debian into the extracted tree. Download the archive from
vendor-sources.json outside the build and run:

    python3 debian/repack-minizipng.py /path/to/minizip-ng-4.2.2.tar.gz ..

The helper verifies its SHA256 and deterministically creates the minizipng orig
component, omitting unused documentation, test fixtures and CI files. Extract
that component under minizipng/ (remove its top-level upstream directory), then
run dpkg-buildpackage -S -sa -us -uc. dpkg-source -x restores both components.

Qualification
-------------

Build native unprivileged and offline with the packaged Qore 3 SDK and declared
Build-Depends. QORE_MINIZIP_SOURCE_DIR selects the offline component. Cross builds
are rejected because Qore tools execute during compilation. Fixed AOT partitions,
prefix maps, timezone and preserved metadata trailers support reproducibility.
Full, -B, -A, nocheck and nodoc profiles are supported.

Run both upstream suites, all compression/encryption feature round trips,
strict provider ownership/locale checks, fresh qcc compilation and qzip/unzip
interoperability. Installed tests copy no source modules. Also qualify source
mode, debug symbols, exact source/resource/catalog parity, minimal runtime
install/purge/reinstall and byte reproducibility across paths and job counts.
No network service is required.

Only Ubuntu 26.04 amd64 with Qore SDK .12 is initially qualified. Other targets,
upgrades from future released packages and the Qore ABI freeze remain release
requirements. Testing PPA publication requires the matching published SDK,
source signing and upload; this is not approval for general release.
